<%- include('partials/head') %>
<body class="ph-body">
  <%- include('partials/nav') %>

  <section class="ph-page-hero">
    <div class="ph-container">
      <div class="ph-eyebrow">Feature deep-dive</div>
      <h1 class="ph-page-title">Your queue, exactly your way.</h1>
      <p class="ph-page-lede">Drag to reorder. Cap the length. Multi-select to download or rate a dozen at once. Auto-play the top recommendation when the queue empties.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ph-section">
    <div class="ph-container ph-feature">
      <div class="ph-feature-copy">
        <h2>Up Next is a real queue.</h2>
        <p>Not a "smart" pile that reshuffles itself when you blink. Episodes go where you put them. They stay there until you play them, finish them, or move them.</p>
        <ul class="ph-checklist">
          <li><strong>Drag-to-reorder</strong> — long-press an episode and drop it where it belongs.</li>
          <li><strong>Currently-playing pin</strong> (optional) — keeps the now-playing episode visually anchored at the top of the queue.</li>
          <li><strong>Total queue duration</strong> displayed at the top so you know how much listening you've lined up.</li>
          <li><strong>Sort options</strong> for any list: date added, publish date, title, more.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <figure class="ph-feature-shot">
        <img src="/public/images/podhaven/up-next.png" alt="Up Next queue showing four queued episodes with total duration of 2h 34m, followed by a Recommended section." loading="lazy">
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ph-section ph-section-alt">
    <div class="ph-container">
      <h2 class="ph-section-title">A maximum length you control.</h2>
      <p class="ph-lede">Set a max queue length anywhere from 10 to 100. PodHaven enforces it. When you add to the top and you're at the cap, the oldest episode at the bottom drops out.</p>
      <p>It's a small thing that fixes a real frustration with other apps: the runaway queue that grows to 400 episodes you'll never get to. Pick a number that matches how you actually listen.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ph-section">
    <div class="ph-container ph-feature ph-feature-flip">
      <div class="ph-feature-copy">
        <h2>Auto-play your top recommendation.</h2>
        <p>You queued five episodes for your commute and finished them halfway home. Instead of falling silent, PodHaven can <strong>auto-play the top recommendation</strong> from the engine — picked freshly when your queue empties.</p>
        <p>Toggle in <em>Settings → Up Next → Auto-play Top Recommendation</em>. Leave it off if you'd rather decide for yourself.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="ph-feature-shot">
        <img src="/public/images/podhaven/up-next.png" alt="Up Next showing a Recommended section beneath the queue — the picks that auto-play would pull from." loading="lazy">
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ph-section ph-section-alt">
    <div class="ph-container">
      <h2 class="ph-section-title">Multi-select, batch actions, swipe shortcuts.</h2>
      <div class="ph-grid">
        <div class="ph-card">
          <h3>Edit mode</h3>
          <p>Tap the pencil icon on any list. Select a dozen episodes. Download them, finish them, rate them, or remove them — one tap, one action, all selected.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ph-card">
          <h3>Swipe actions</h3>
          <p>Swipe left to delete, save, or mark finished. Swipe right for additional actions. Faster than opening the row.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ph-card">
          <h3>Long-press menus</h3>
          <p>Hold an episode anywhere in the app for a context menu with rating, queue placement, downloads, and sharing.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ph-card">
          <h3>Auto-queue from a podcast</h3>
          <p>For shows you never want to miss, set <em>Queue All Episodes → On Top</em> in the per-podcast settings. New episodes jump straight onto your queue. <a class="ph-inline-link" href="/podhaven/guides/per-podcast-settings#queue">How to →</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%- include('partials/footer') %>
